{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE NAVIGATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Shows the prev next articles for a given blog post.

* show_date
* show_author
* show_comments_count
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="article-navigation">
  <h2 class="article-navigation__title text-with-icon h4">{%- render 'icon' with 'blog-nav-right', width: 19, height: 20, direction_aware: true -%} {{ 'blog.post.continue_reading' | t }}</h2>

  <div class="article-prev-next scroll-area bleed sm:unbleed">
    {%- comment -%}Performance (2026-10-13): these two cards sit below the whole article, so their images are lazy-loaded (blog-post-card loads a card image lazily when its position is above 3). They no longer download at page start next to the article banner image (the LCP element); the browser fetches them before they are scrolled into view, so they look and behave exactly as before.{%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if blog.previous_article -%}
      {%- render 'blog-post-card', article: blog.previous_article, heading_size: 'h5', show_date: section.settings.show_date, show_author: section.settings.show_author, show_comments_count: show_comments_count, position: 4 -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if blog.next_article -%}
      {%- render 'blog-post-card', article: blog.next_article, heading_size: 'h5', show_date: section.settings.show_date, show_author: section.settings.show_author, show_comments_count: show_comments_count, position: 4 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>